From: CreckerROM <creckerrom@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Hide unsupported 24 FPS Pro Video modes on tele

Exynos990 tele sessions fail at 8K, UHD and FHD 24 FPS in Pro Video.
Filter those modes from the rear Pro Video resolution picker while a
tele lens is selected, including cinema ratios, and reject stale clicks.
Use the per-ratio default resolution for saved unsupported tele settings
before configuring the camera session. Before a tele lens switch, reset
the stored unsupported resolutions through the normal settings path so
the engine receives the resolution change before the lens change. Keep
the other lenses and ordinary Video resolution lists unchanged.

---
--- a/smali_classes4/com/sec/android/app/camera/util/CameraResolution.smali
+++ b/smali_classes4/com/sec/android/app/camera/util/CameraResolution.smali
@@ -4121,10 +4121,58 @@

